How to Run on MacOS or Linux:

    Download GTK-3 (with homebrew): brew install gtk+3

    Compile Command: gcc src/*.c -Iinclude -o main $(pkg-config --cflags --libs gtk+-3.0)

    Run Program: ./main

How to Run on Windows:

    1. INSTALL MSYS2
       - Download MSYS2 from: https://www.msys2.org
       - Install it to the default location: C:\msys64
       - Open “MSYS2 MSYS” from the Start Menu.
       - Update the system:
           pacman -Syuu
       - If it asks to restart, close the window and run the command again until no updates remain.

    2. INSTALL THE MINGW-W64 TOOLCHAIN AND GTK3
       - Open “MSYS2 MinGW x64” (IMPORTANT: not the MSYS shell).
       - The terminal prompt must show: MINGW64 ~
       - Install the compiler and GTK3:
           pacman -S --needed base-devel mingw-w64-x86_64-toolchain
           pacman -S --needed mingw-w64-x86_64-gtk3
       - Verify GTK installation:
           pkg-config --cflags --libs gtk+-3.0
         You should see a long list of include paths and libraries.

    3. NAVIGATE TO THE PROJECT FOLDER
       - Still inside MSYS2 MinGW x64, go to the project directory:
           cd /c/path/to/your/project

    4. COMPILE THE PROJECT
       - Run this command from the project root (to paste on MINGW press "insert" button):
gcc \
  src/main.c \
  src/create_queue.c \
  src/enqueue.c \
  src/dequeue.c \
  src/free_queue.c \
  src/is_empty.c \
  src/output.c \
  src/validation.c \
  src/peek.c \
  src/queue_to_string.c \
  -Iinclude \
  `pkg-config --cflags --libs gtk+-3.0` \
  -o emergency_room.exe
    5. RUN THE APPLICATION
       - In the same terminal:
           ./emergency_room.exe
